  "changelog": "v106: connectors: calibrated external-evidence ingestion, Gmail first (issue #44). New system/connectors/ framework: a permanent metadata ledger (state/connectors/gmail_ledger.jsonl, no bodies) + cursor; connector-fetch appends new metadata, connector-excavate re-scores the ENTIRE ledger against the current wiki/rosters/sources every run (scores never trusted across runs — relevance flips promote old mail without re-fetching), refreshes gmail_date_evidence.json, mines unknown people/threads/institutions into question_candidates.json (provenance connector-mined), and delta-promotes above-threshold threads into immutable sources/gmail/ external_record sources (idempotent by message id, per-run cap, --dry-run, connector-audit). Six deterministic scoring axes with weights/thresholds versioned in state/connectors/weights.json; connector-calibrate writes the Phase 2 shadow report (state/reports/gmail_calibration.md) and records the chosen threshold. gmail.readonly scope only; google SDK imports are lazy; OAuth token gitignored. New CLI: connector-auth/fetch/excavate/report/audit/calibrate via system/connector.py.",
